1
00:00:04,953 --> 00:00:07,549
WELCOME TO SPACE TO GROUND, I’M CHELSEY
BALLARTE.

2
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:11,240
CAN YOU BELIEVE IT’S BEEN 5 YEARS SINCE
THE ADVANCED PLANT HABITAT

3
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:13,860
LAUNCHED TO THE INTERNATIONAL SPACE STATION?

4
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:14,860
SINCE 2017,

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:18,910
THE HABITAT HAS GROWN WHEAT, RADDISHES, CHILI
PEPPERS…

6
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:20,180
AND WE’RE JUST GETTING STARTED.

7
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:24,890
THIS WEEK ON THE SPACE STATION, THE ASTRONAUTS
ARE PREPPING THE HABITAT FOR ITS NEXT EXPERIMENT.

8
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:28,470
THIS UPCOMING EXPERIMENT LOOKS AT WHETHER
GENE ADAPTATIONS

9
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:33,969
IN ONE GENERATION OF PLANTS GROWN IN SPACE
CAN TRANSFER TO THE NEXT GENERATION.

10
00:00:33,969 --> 00:00:37,809
STUDYING PLANT ADAPATABILITY NOT ONLY HELPS
RESEARCHERS BETTER PREPARE ASTRONAUTS

11
00:00:37,809 --> 00:00:40,609
FOR GROWING FOOD DURING LONG DURATION MISSIONS
ON THE MOON,

12
00:00:40,609 --> 00:00:44,959
BUT IT CAN ALSO PROVIDE LESSONS AND TECHNOLOGIES
THAT COULD IMPROVE FARMING METHODS HERE ON

13
00:00:44,959 --> 00:00:46,289
EARTH.

14
00:00:46,289 --> 00:00:49,499
WHILE ASTRONAUTS ARE STUDYING WAYS TO GROW
THEIR OWN FOOD,

15
00:00:49,499 --> 00:00:53,199
MOST OF THEIR MEALS ARE DELIVERED USING A
CARGO SPACECRAFT.

16
00:00:53,199 --> 00:00:57,570
ONE FREIGHTER HAS NEARLY COMPLETED ITS DELIVERY
AND IS SET TO COME BACK HOME NEXT WEEK.

17
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:02,069
SPACEX’S 25TH COMMERCIAL RESUPPLY SERVICES
MISSION ARRIVED AT THE SPACE STATION

18
00:01:02,069 --> 00:01:08,039
BACK IN JULY AND DELIVERED NEARLY 6,000 POUNDS
OF SCIENCE AND SUPPLIES TO THE CREW IN ORBIT.

19
00:01:08,039 --> 00:01:11,700
NOW NEARING THE END OF ITS MISSION, THE CREW
HAS BEEN TASKED THIS WEEK WITH PACKING

20
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,060
THE CARGO DRAGON FOR ITS RETURN TRIP BACK
TO EARTH.

21
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:17,850
CARGO DRAGON WILL RETURN SAMPLES FROM EXPERIMENTS
CONDUCTED

22
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:21,370
ON THE ORBITING LAB FOR ANALYSIS BY RESEARCHERS
ON THE GROUND.

23
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:23,670
BE SURE TO KEEP UP WITH THE SPACE STATION
BLOG,

24
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:29,579
AND FOLLOW @SPACE_STATION FOR WHEN WATCH THE
UNDOCKING LIVE ON NASA TV.

25
00:01:29,579 --> 00:01:32,979
ALSO COMING UP NEXT WEEK, TWO RUSSIAN COSMONAUTS
ARE SUITING UP

26
00:01:32,979 --> 00:01:36,180
AND HEADING OUTSIDE OF THE SPACE STATION FOR
A SPACEWALK.

27
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:39,579
OLEG ARTEMYEV AND DENIS MATVEYEV WILL SPEND
NEARLY SEVEN HOURS

28
00:01:39,579 --> 00:01:43,000
WORKING ON THE EUROPEAN ROBOTIC ARM TO INSTALL
CAMERAS,

29
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,749
REMOVE EQUIPMENT USED DURING THE ARM’S LAUNCH,
AND MORE.

30
00:01:45,749 --> 00:01:50,759
THIS WILL BE THE SEVENTH SPACEWALK FOR ARTEMYEV,
AND THE THIRD FOR MATVEYEV.

31
00:01:50,759 --> 00:01:55,310
ARTEMYEV COMPLETED A SPACEWALK WITH EUROPEAN
SPACE AGENCY ASTRONAUT SAMANTHA CRISTOFORETTI

32
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:57,200
JUST LAST MONTH.

33
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,299
WHILE OUT ON SPACEWALKS, THE CREWMEMBERS ARE
BUSY

34
00:01:59,299 --> 00:02:02,240
WITH THEIR TASKS, BUT SOMETIMES TAKE A MOMENT
TO LOOK DOWN

35
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,219
AT THE BEAUTY OF THE EARTH BELOW THEM.

36
00:02:04,219 --> 00:02:07,079
FORTUNATELY, WE DON’T HAVE TO WAIT UNTIL
THE NEXT SPACEWALK

37
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:10,399
TO CATCH A GLIMPSE OF WHAT THEY’RE SEEING
THOUGH THEIR EYES.

38
00:02:10,399 --> 00:02:14,860
NASA JUST RELEASED VIEWS OF THE EARTH CAPTURED
FROM THE INTERNATIONAL SPACE STATION,

39
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:17,370
AVAILABLE IN 4K RESOLUTION.

40
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:20,040
IN NEARLY ONE HOUR OF CLIPS SHOT IN 2021,

41
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:23,959
YOU’LL FIND SPACECRAFT ARRIVING AND DEPARTING,
AURORAS,

42
00:02:23,959 --> 00:02:26,090
CITY LIGHTS AT NIGHT, AND MUCH MORE.

43
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:29,440
JUST HIT PLAY, SIT BACK, AND ENJOY.

44
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,959
AND THAT’S SPACE TO GROUND.

45
00:02:30,959 --> 00:02:31,959
THANKS SO MUCH FOR WATCHING.

46
00:02:31,959 --> 00:02:33,444
WE’LL SEE YOU NEXT WEEK.

